  "question": {
    "text": "In the Coolidge tube experiment, if the applied voltage is increased to three times, the short wavelength limit of continuous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>ray</mi></math> spectrum shifts by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pm</mi></math>. What is the initial voltage (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kV</mi></math>) applied to the tube?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "41",
  "solution": {
